        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Method A (aerobic): to a stirred solution of [Fe3O((CH3)3CCO2)6(H2O)2(OH)]·H2O (0.1 g, 0.117 mmol) in 15 mL CH3CN were added (NH4)2Ce(NO3)6 (0.064 g, 0.117 mmol), CH3CO2Na (0.010 g, 0.117 mmol) and Hap (0.045 mL, 0.583 mmol). The greenish solution was stirred for 30 min, filtered, and left undisturbed in closed vials at room temperature. After 10 days orange X-ray quality needles were collected, washed with CH3CN and dried under vacuum. Method B: FeCl3 (0.1 g, 0.616 mmol) in 15 mL CH3CN with (CH3)3CCO2H (0.126 g, 1.233 mmol), (NH4)2Ce(NO3)6 (0.338 g, 0.616 mmol), CH3CO2Na (0.051 g, 0.616 mmol) and Hap (0.141 mL, 1.849 mmol); stirred 30 min, filtered, stood at room temperature; orange needles after one week.",
