      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility of 1·4H2O (0.1 T, 5–300 K) shows χMT ≈ 16.60 cm3 mol−1 K at 300 K, nearly constant to 50 K, then falling to 13.66 cm3 mol−1 K at 5 K, slightly below the spin-only value for four non-interacting HS Fe(III) ions (17.50 cm3 mol−1 K; Ce(IV) diamagnetic). The profile indicates very weak/negligible Fe···Fe coupling, consistent with Fe···Fe separations of ~7.0 Å. Ac data show a further small χMT decrease from 14.0 cm3 mol−1 K at 10 K to 10.5 cm3 mol−1 K at 1.8 K.",
